<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        A comment placed ABOVE <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the
        misleading error "unable to find matching parent xml file for CustomField". Precedent:
        Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml.

        THE TOKEN CONTRACT - IDENTICAL TO LOI__c.Ball_In_Court__c, AND THE TWO MUST BE READ
        TOGETHER because CounterOfferService flips one from the other:

          Ours   = DPEG. Correct on BOTH sides - side-neutral, like Ball_In_Court__c's 'Us'.
          Seller = THE COUNTERPARTY, ON BOTH SIDES. This is the INCUMBENT WIRE TOKEN the
                   deployed lwc/loiCounterOffer picker already sends; it must keep being
                   accepted on a sale or that Save button dies against a restricted picklist.
          Buyer  = THE COUNTERPARTY, DISPOSITION ONLY. Added 2026-08-09.

        ADD ONLY - NOTHING IS RENAMED. A picklist rename is a removal plus an add: it triggers
        the standing picklist-removal sweep rule and forces a data migration on live acquisition
        counter-offer rows for zero benefit. This field is <restricted>true</restricted>, so the
        value must exist in the master value set before Apex can write it - four tests were
        failing INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST against exactly this gap.

        Counter_Offer__c HAS NO RECORD TYPES, so unlike LOI__c.Ball_In_Court__c there is no
        per-type restriction available here and all three values are selectable on every counter
        offer. Directionality is therefore enforced by the SERVICE, not by metadata: the parent
        LOI's record type decides which token is written. Do not read the presence of 'Buyer' on
        an acquisition counter offer as sanctioned - it is unreachable through the UI the service
        drives, not blocked by the platform.
    -->
    <fullName>Direction__c</fullName>
    <description>Who made this counter. Ours = DPEG on either side. Seller = the counterparty on either side, and the incumbent wire token. Buyer = the counterparty on a disposition LOI only. Drives the ball-in-court flip and the counter notifications.</description>
    <label>Direction</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>Seller</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Seller</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Ours</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Ours</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Buyer</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Buyer</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
